# Prompt delivery (copy-paste)

When the operator asks for prompts to send to another coding agent — parallel streams, handoffs,
"give me the prompt", "stream A and B", or after a mode B setup — **deliver each prompt as one
fenced code block**, ready to copy in one click.

## Required format

### Single slice

One fenced block holding the **entire** prompt, in the `═══` sections of
[`implementation_prompt.md`](/.ai/tickets/implementation_prompt.md). A one-line intro above the
block is fine; **do not** split the prompt across prose paragraphs.

### Parallel streams (for example two independent slices, both on `main`)

**Exactly N code blocks for N streams** — typically **two**:

1. A short heading: `# Stream A — <slice id> <title>`, and a working-directory line (repository
   root, `main`)
2. **One complete fenced block** with the full prompt (everything the agent needs)
3. A short heading: `# Stream B — …`
4. **One complete fenced block** with the full prompt

Streams share `main` by default; the only per-ticket branches are the factory's `slice/<id>`
worktrees, which the xtask tooling creates ([Factory waves](/documentation_v2/runbooks/factory_waves/README.md)).
A preflight shell block may follow as an optional extra block at the end — never in place of the
prompt blocks.

## Forbidden

- Summarizing the prompt in prose instead of a copy-paste block
- "See the handoff" as the only deliverable when the operator asked for the prompt
- One block with both streams concatenated without clear separation
- Partial prompts ("run these commands, then ask for part 2")
- Bullet lists that repeat content **outside** the fenced block when the operator wanted the full
  prompt

## Source of truth

Build the prompt from the spec's `## Claude Code prompt` block (the heading
`cargo xtask ticket prompt <id>` reads), the handoff `.ai/artifacts/<slug>_claude_code_handoff.md`
when one exists (`cargo xtask ticket prompt <id> --header` prints its path), and
`cargo xtask ticket brief <id>`. If `ticket prompt` fails because the spec has no prompt block,
**still** output the full block built from the spec, the handoff and the brief — do not tell the
operator to run the command instead of pasting.

## Example shape (parallel)

````markdown
# Stream A — <slice id> <slice title>

**Working directory:** repository root (`main`)

```text
{full prompt — PREFLIGHT, READ, PROBLEM, DO, DO NOT, VERIFY, RETURN}
```

# Stream B — <slice id> <slice title>

**Working directory:** repository root (`main`)

```text
{full prompt — PREFLIGHT, READ, PROBLEM, DO, DO NOT, VERIFY, RETURN}
```
````
